  "706-712 Army Avn Fixed Wing Ac, Army Avn Hels, Armed / Unarmed Hels - Performance Data/Emp: on the 31 weapons.json entries (section Sec 7 - Avn), re-checked figure by figure on 15 Nov 2026, no differences; types by possible role in avnData",
  "713 Reqs of Helipads: in avnData (req a-k, reception a-e, marking of wires: orange streamers at 5 Ms interval)",
  "714 Load/Cas Evac Cap - Army Avn Hels: in avnData and on the 7 hel entries in weapons.json (loadCasEvac)",
  "715 Engagement Tech of Cbt Avn (diagram): in avnData and summarised in avn-sqn-cbt notes"
 ],
 "dataNotes": [
  "p 708: The lift cap of all hels can be enhanced if fuel is reduced; however, the endurance and range would reduce proportionately. External load means the max lift cap of the hel using sling; in such case the internal load would be compromised.",
  "pp 710, 712: Ref to C&SC Basic Book on Avn for performance data/emp of other imp armed / unarmed hels. Auth (unarmed hels): Jane's All the Worlds Aircraft.",
  "Speeds: Army Avn Fixed Wing Ac and Army Avn Hels tables give normal cruising speed (cruiseSpeedKmph); the armed / unarmed performance tables give max speed (maxSpeedKmph). Ceilings: H = Hovering, S = Svc."
 ],
